Patagonia's Supply Chain Environmental Responsibility Program exemplifies transparent and sustainable supply chain management. The Footprint Chronicles provide detailed information about product origins and environmental/social impacts at each production stage. Patagonia publishes its complete supplier list online with facility coordinates and voluntarily discloses production information. The company has achieved 93% recycled polyester and 89% recycled nylon in products while participating in foundational industry collaborations including the Higg Index, Textile Exchange, and Regenerative Organic Alliance. This comprehensive traceability enables customers to understand environmental footprints, demonstrating how transparency drives accountability and sustainable supply chain transformation at scale.